  Enhanced Mobile Search Popup Usage Guide
  
  The mobile search popup now includes:
  
  1. Professional tire image (P21560R16-sidewall.jpg) at the top
  2. Page-aware title that changes based on current page context
  3. Three filter dropdowns: Type, Size, and Brand
  4. Automatic population from URL parameters and collection tags
  5. Triggerable from any button or link
  
  ## How to trigger search popup from any button:
  
  Method 1: Add the data attribute manually
  <button data-trigger-search="winter-tires">Winter Tires</button>
  <button data-trigger-search="summer-tires">Summer Tires</button>
  <button data-trigger-search="all-season-tires">All-Season Tires</button>
  
  Method 2: Use the search-trigger snippet
  <button {% include 'search-trigger', search_context: 'winter-tires' %}>Winter Tires</button>
  
  Method 3: Call JavaScript function directly
  <button onclick="openMobileSearchWithContext('winter-tires')">Winter Tires</button>
  
  ## Automatic Features:
  
  - Dropdowns are automatically populated with common options
  - If on a collection page, dropdowns are enhanced with actual collection tags
  - URL parameters are automatically parsed and dropdowns are pre-selected
  - Search title updates based on page context (e.g., "Search Winter Tires" on winter tire pages)
  - Mobile menu items containing tire-related terms automatically become search triggers
  
  ## Supported Search Contexts:
  
  - winter, winter-tires: Pre-selects Winter type
  - summer, summer-tires: Pre-selects Summer type  
  - all-season, all-season-tires: Pre-selects All-Season type
  - Any other context: Opens search without pre-selection
  
{% endcomment %}
